  "body": "## What this builds (#6032 remainder)\n\nSlice 1 (decision layer, PR #7788) and rung 4 (escalation, PR #8357) already landed. This PR builds the rest of the watchdog core:\n\n- **`src/watchdog.ts`** — the oneshot entry point. Per tick: load adapters, read the state file through `coerceHealth`, observe each source (producer document + gatherer heartbeat + live CDP liveness probe), classify (including missing-document, stale-read-while-the-browser-lives, and dead-CDP — the classes the producer cannot see itself), `decide`, execute the rung, run rung-4 escalation/recovery, write state back atomically (tmp+rename), append `quota-watchdog-history.jsonl`. Nothing decision-relevant lives in process memory (#5928).\n- **Rung executors** — rung 2: CDP re-validation (`/json/version` + `/json/list`, allowlist origin open, cookies present **by name** via the CDP websocket — values never enter the process) with one bounded supervised restart of the adapter's browser unit; rung 3: re-login driver that stops dead at a human-only challenge and marks the incident human-blocked. Repairs are gated on `QUOTA_WATCHDOG_LIVE_REPAIRS=1`, rung-4 production effectors (fleet queue / `gh`) on `QUOTA_WATCHDOG_LIVE=1`; the systemd unit sets both, a bare CLI run journals dry-run plans and creates nothing.\n- **`src/adapters.ts` + `adapters/fixture.json`** — the adapter loader: per-provider JSON (origins allowlist, CDP port, data paths, cookie names, login hints, class/rung maps, thresholds), structurally validated, defects reported per file instead of throwing. The core contains zero provider names; the fixture adapter is the one shipped here, real provider adapters are follow-ons per the issue scope.\n- **`producers/producer-template.mjs`** — forkable producer scaffold from the retired Meta producer pattern (timeout-bounded CDP, tab ownership, failure-class exit codes + failure documents, atomic `latest.json`), plus `test/fixtures/fixture-producer.mjs`, the scenario-driven stub the acceptance tests drive.\n- **`pm-stack/systemd/pm-quota-watchdog.{service,timer}`** — oneshot + timer on the gatherer cadence, offset to `*:3/15`.\n\n## Tests (oracles named per the testing doctrine)\n\n`bun test ../exporters/test/` — **35 pass, 0 fail** (includes the pre-existing state + escalation suites). The new `test/watchdog.test.ts` drives the entry point end to end against a scratch tree:\n\n- broken source walks retry → CDP re-validation → re-login → escalation, caps honored (no rung >2× per incident), escalates exactly once and dedupes on later ticks;\n- rate-limited fixture sets `cooldownUntil` on disk and a fresh tick honors it with no repair action (the #5928 regression shape);\n- human-only challenge fixture marks the incident human-blocked with the surfacing flag and a same-tick NEEDS DREW line, and the ladder stops dead;\n- healthy source is quiet (state + history only, no output);\n- recovery after escalation comments/closes/completes the hand-off;\n- cross-invocation persistence: every tick re-reads state from disk.\n\nCLI fixture demo also run live: healthy tick quiet; `session-expired` scenario classified and rung 3 recorded (as `skipped` with live repairs off).\n\nLive install (units + timer + a laptop-local adapter for the Meta file-export source) and the ≥3-consecutive-tick demonstration follow the merge and are reported on #6032.\n\nTask 19956 · lane any-k\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797505200&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11243&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11243&signature=1b6f044ebd855a16f55dd8963cf4591666c1bd3f183f86b04e381c0f43e32ecb\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/11243?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
